## Original Content
What a new round of U.S. sanctions could mean after nearly six months of war with Iran — and years of economic pressure on the country.

## Summary
The article explores whether a new round of U.S. economic sanctions against Iran could succeed where military airstrikes and diplomatic negotiations have failed. It analyzes the potential implications after months of conflict and long-standing economic pressure on Iran.

## Key Points
- U.S. sanctions on Iran are escalating as a key economic warfare strategy.
- Sanctions are being evaluated in comparison to airstrikes and negotiations.
- The context includes ongoing conflict and years of economic pressure on Iran.
- The article assesses the potential effectiveness and outcomes of these sanctions.


